# Trivy Ignore - Known False Positives and Accepted Risks
#
# Format: VulnerabilityID    ExpiryDate    Reason
#
# Add entries below when Trivy reports CVEs that are:
#   1. False positives (not actually exploitable in our context)
#   2. Accepted risks (mitigated by other controls)
#   3. Fixed in an upstream dependency but not yet in our base image
#
# Example:
# CVE-2023-12345   2026-12-31   False positive - only affects interactive session, not our use case